 "background": null,
 "description": "FPS — real frames per second, measured on the wall clock, plus the virtual cycle rate derived through the skip ratio. The top-line health number for the prime goal (many planets at constant 60). ScreenGov detects the display's true refresh; target fps derives from it, never a hardcoded 60. If FPS is low but virtual is high, skips are hiding pain; by the Pure Frames Law prefer fixing cost over skipping frames."
